    <node id="Leroror Lukaine">
      <data key="d0">Leroror Lukaine</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Leroror Lukaine is a senior employee at Zastama Industries who joined the company in 2015 and serves as a key figure in its organizational structure. She is the individual to whom Zosu Kistos reports and is responsible for making decisions regarding the work Zosu Kistos is involved in. As a manager, Leroror Lukaine oversees Zosu Kistos and acts as a point of contact for approvals and questions related to their work. She also provides guidance to both Zosu Kistos and Fallem Purraren, reinforcing her role as a central figure in the company's operations.

In addition to her managerial responsibilities, Leroror Lukaine is the Research Lead for Project Nuzeor, a position in which she leads the project and communicates its outcomes to the wider company. She is also the designated contact for any work that overlaps with or could be affected by vendor renewals, highlighting her role in cross-functional coordination. Leroror Lukaine is a member of the Dankenor Analytics Unit and has participated in meetings where she raised questions about the prioritization of incoming requests, demonstrating her involvement in strategic decision-making processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The leader of Project Nuzeor, responsible for setting priorities, removing obstacles, and keeping stakeholders informed.&lt;SEP&gt;Leroror Lukaine is the person to whom Zosu Kistos reports. Leroror is included in the memo as the escalation contact for unresolved matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-012-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-015-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-011-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-014-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-002&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-001&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-004&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-006&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-012&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-015&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-018&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-011&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-014</data>
      <data key="d5">1793369436</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vadesis Gummenbel">
      <data key="d0">Vadesis Gummenbel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Vadesis Gummenbel is a Chief of Staff at Zastama Industries and a member of the Dankenor Analytics Unit. In their role, they support cross-functional coordination, communication, and decision recording across the company. Vadesis facilitates meetings, ensures communication clarity, and helps coordinate priorities among different groups. They are also responsible for circulating notes to all employees and scheduling cross-functional updates.

As a key contact for unclear requests or workstreams, Vadesis Gummenbel serves as a first point of contact for issues that lack clear ownership. They have sent company-wide clarifications on analytics funding and project ownership and have responded to follow-up inquiries from a Finance Lead. Additionally, they provide feedback on the feasibility of data retention approaches for Project Soramis and have commented on seating arrangements for Project Nolaor.

Beyond their internal coordination duties, Vadesis is one of the contacts for questions related to the usage data of vendors' services, further highlighting their role in bridging operational and analytical functions within the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Vadesis Gummenbel is a person who reports to Zosne Bramfa and is involved in the day-to-day delivery of the Gaskergur Harbor engagement.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual responsible for data retention tooling and reporting to Zosne Bramfa. The escrow reference for Vadesis Gummenbel is WX-1844-U.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-005-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-015-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-009-chunk-000</data>
