      <data key="d5">1793351056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dankenor Analytics Unit">
      <data key="d0">Dankenor Analytics Unit</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Dankenor Analytics Unit is a department within Zastama Industries responsible for a wide range of analytics-related functions across the company. It operates on an annual budget of $6.4M and is composed of 38 members who provide data-driven insights to support forecasting, decision-making, and business strategy. The unit blends data analysis with engineering practice, working on identity and access tooling, shared dataset documentation, and the development of internal analytics infrastructure.

One of its key responsibilities is fleet telemetry, where it collects, processes, and reports telemetry data back to the business, serving as the primary point of contact for all telemetry-related inquiries and requests. Additionally, the unit is tasked with analyzing how heavily each vendor's services are used, offering insights that inform resource allocation and vendor management strategies.

The Dankenor Analytics Unit also plays a central role in governance and project sponsorship, particularly for initiatives such as Project Stebril, which it owns and oversees. It provides governance, prioritization, and escalation paths for the project. The unit supports teams across the company with analysis and reporting, and is the right place to begin for questions about reports, data analysis, and decision-informing data. It is led by members such as Pivoine Geltoett and is recognized as a critical internal resource for both quantitative and qualitative research and analytics work.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit at Zastama Industries responsible for handling analytics-related requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-009-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-016-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-019-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-007-chunk-000</data>
