    <node id="Action Items">
      <data key="d0">Action Items</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Action Items are specific tasks assigned to individuals or groups during or following a meeting for follow-up and completion. These tasks are typically outlined to ensure continuity, alignment, and progress on key objectives. Attendees are often given responsibilities such as drafting exception categories, confirming model requirements, building renewal calendars, reviewing contracts, documenting technical requirements, collecting input, flagging risks, and reviewing materials. Action Items may also include governance-related tasks identified in the reporting section of a document. The primary purpose of these items is to ensure that all participants are clear on their responsibilities and that necessary actions are completed before the next meeting or synchronization point. They are commonly documented in meeting notes or action plans to track accountability and progress.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-007-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-003-chunk-000</data>
