      <data key="d2">A designated individual responsible for managing the vendor relationship with Misginine Systems on behalf of Zastama Industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Decision summaries">
      <data key="d0">Decision summaries</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Summaries of what was agreed upon during the meeting, to be distributed to all locations simultaneously.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agendas">
      <data key="d0">Agendas</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Meeting agendas that will be sent out ahead of time to ensure all locations are equally informed.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Next steps">
      <data key="d0">Next steps</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The follow-up actions and reporting requirements for meeting owners, including progress updates at the next sync.&lt;SEP&gt;A section of the report outlining the planned actions for the upcoming period.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-011-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-011</data>
      <data key="d5">1793369393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-functional sessions">
      <data key="d0">Cross-functional sessions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A series of meetings, including the one on October 9, 2026, aimed at aligning teams and sharing information across departments.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-functional Sessions">
      <data key="d0">Cross-functional Sessions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Sessions involving multiple departments or functions within an organization, from which notes are published by Zastama Industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Operations Lead">
      <data key="d0">Operations Lead</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual responsible for handling operations-related inquiries or actions, such as contacting for material distribution or site-related matters.&lt;SEP&gt;A stakeholder in Project Siduris who has been briefed and has not raised blocking objections.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-004-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-004</data>
      <data key="d5">1793351316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Owner">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Owner</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual designated as the owner of certain materials or responsibilities, to be contacted for matters related to their site or distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-018-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-018</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Demand Forecasting">
      <data key="d0">Demand Forecasting</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Demand Forecasting is a focus area within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. It involves creating models to predict future demand for products or services.&lt;SEP&gt;Demand Forecasting is the process of predicting future demand, which is a focus area for Liluan Nemlurel.&lt;SEP&gt;Demand Forecasting is the process of predicting future demand. It is the central focus of the workstream and involves modeling, assumptions, and validation against actual demand.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003</data>
      <data key="d5">1793351727</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Technical Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Architecture is a focus area within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. It involves designing how data, tools, and models should fit together to support business decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Coordination and Priorities">
      <data key="d0">Coordination and Priorities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Coordination and Priorities is a focus area within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. It involves managing workstreams, stakeholder communication, and ensuring that requests are handled efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reporting Relationships">
      <data key="d0">Reporting Relationships</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reporting Relationships refer to the hierarchical structure within the organization that defines who reports to whom. These relationships are key for determining who can approve requests, reprioritize work, or be copied on decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Analytics Requests">
      <data key="d0">Analytics Requests</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Analytics Requests are inquiries or tasks submitted to the Dankenor Analytics Unit for support in forecasting, data analysis, or technical design.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Working Norms">
      <data key="d0">Working Norms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Working Norms are the standard practices and expectations within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. These include prompt acknowledgment of requests, clear communication, documentation of models, and openness to feedback.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Forecasting Models">
      <data key="d0">Forecasting Models</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Forecasting Models are tools or systems developed by the Dankenor Analytics Unit to predict future demand or trends. These models are supported by architectural design and are used to inform business decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Forecasting Models are the models used by Liluan Nemlurel to predict demand, which are sensitive to the timing of recorded payments.&lt;SEP&gt;Forecasting Models refer to the models used for demand forecasting. These models are the focus of Thikama Harlurine's work and are discussed in a restricted channel.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003</data>
      <data key="d5">1793351727</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Design">
      <data key="d0">Technical Design</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Design refers to the process of planning and structuring the systems, tools, and models used in analytics work. It is a key area of focus for the unit, especially in the early stages of a project.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Solutions Architect">
      <data key="d0">Solutions Architect</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Solutions Architect is a role within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. The person in this role, such as Munnam Furzil, is responsible for advising on how data, tools, and models should be integrated to support business decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A role responsible for designing and integrating systems and infrastructure solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The role title assigned to Liluan Nemlurel, which needs to be recorded consistently across systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793351234</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Forecasting Work">
      <data key="d0">Forecasting Work</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Forecasting Work refers to the tasks and projects undertaken by the Dankenor Analytics Unit to develop and maintain demand forecasting models. This work is supported by architectural design and stakeholder coordination.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Data Questions">
      <data key="d0">Data Questions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Questions are inquiries related to data analysis, interpretation, or modeling that are addressed by the Dankenor Analytics Unit. These questions are often raised by employees across Zastama Industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Analytics Support">
      <data key="d0">Analytics Support</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Analytics Support refers to the assistance provided by the Dankenor Analytics Unit to other teams within Zastama Industries. This includes forecasting, data modeling, and technical design.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Scoping">
      <data key="d0">Request Scoping</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Scoping is the process of defining the boundaries and objectives of an analytics request. The unit may suggest a smaller first step to ensure value is delivered early and adjustments can be made before further effort is invested.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Early Collaboration">
      <data key="d0">Early Collaboration</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Early Collaboration is a recommended practice for teams within Zastama Industries to involve the Dankenor Analytics Unit at the initial stages of a project. This helps in shaping the question and ensuring that the work is aligned with business needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Page Owner">
      <data key="d0">Page Owner</data>
      <data key="d1">role</data>
      <data key="d2">Page Owner is the person responsible for maintaining the accuracy and relevance of the information on the Dankenor Analytics Unit's overview page. They are to be informed of any gaps or errors in the content.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual responsible for maintaining the restricted working notes and ensuring their accuracy and appropriate distribution at Zastama Industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-003-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-003</data>
      <data key="d5">1793369501</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Model Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Model Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Model Documentation is the practice of recording how forecasting or analytical models work so that others can understand and use them. This is a key working norm within the Dankenor Analytics Unit.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Healthy Skepticism">
      <data key="d0">Healthy Skepticism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Healthy Skepticism is encouraged among colleagues outside the Dankenor Analytics Unit to challenge results and improve the quality of work. This builds trust and ensures that the work is robust and reliable.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planning Horizon">
      <data key="d0">Planning Horizon</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Planning Horizon refers to the time frame over which a forecast or planning activity is conducted. It is an important context to provide when making forecasting requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Known Disruptions">
      <data key="d0">Known Disruptions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Known Disruptions are events or factors that are expected to impact demand or operations. These should be included in forecasting requests to ensure accurate modeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Owner">
      <data key="d0">Request Owner</data>
      <data key="d1">role</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Owner is the person from the requesting team who is responsible for answering follow-up questions and ensuring that the analytics request is handled smoothly.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Decision-Making">
      <data key="d0">Decision-Making</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Decision-Making is the process of using analytics to inform business choices. The Dankenor Analytics Unit supports this by providing evidence-based insights and models.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Workstream">
      <data key="d0">Workstream</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Workstream refers to a specific line of work or project within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. It is used to categorize and manage different types of analytics requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prioritization">
      <data key="d0">Prioritization</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prioritization is the process of determining the order in which analytics requests are handled. It is managed by the Chief of Staff and is essential for efficient resource allocation.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Model Behavior">
      <data key="d0">Model Behavior</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Model Behavior refers to how a forecasting or analytical model functions and produces results. It is documented so that others can understand and use the model effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Change Notification">
      <data key="d0">Change Notification</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Change Notification is the process of informing stakeholders when a forecast or model changes significantly. This ensures that those relying on the information are aware of the update.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Jargon-Free Communication">
      <data key="d0">Jargon-Free Communication</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Jargon-Free Communication is a working norm within the Dankenor Analytics Unit. It involves explaining results and models in plain language to ensure clarity and accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Assumption Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Assumption Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Assumption Documentation is the practice of writing down the assumptions made during an analytics project. This helps ensure transparency and allows for better decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Submission">
      <data key="d0">Request Submission</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Submission is the process of submitting an analytics request to the Dankenor Analytics Unit. It is encouraged to include context and details to help the unit understand the needs and goals.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Early Conversations">
      <data key="d0">Early Conversations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Early Conversations are discussions between teams and the Dankenor Analytics Unit at the initial stages of a project. These help in scoping and prioritizing work more effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Model Adjustment">
      <data key="d0">Model Adjustment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Model Adjustment is the process of modifying a forecasting or analytical model based on feedback or new information. It is part of the iterative process of improving model accuracy and relevance.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Value Delivery">
      <data key="d0">Value Delivery</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Value Delivery is the goal of ensuring that analytics work provides tangible benefits to the requesting team. The unit may suggest smaller initial steps to deliver value sooner and allow for adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Clarification">
      <data key="d0">Request Clarification</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Clarification is the process of understanding the details and objectives of an analytics request. It is important to describe the decision being made and what success looks like.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Outcome Sharing">
      <data key="d0">Outcome Sharing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Outcome Sharing is the practice of informing the Dankenor Analytics Unit how the results of their work were used. This feedback helps improve future projects and ensures alignment with business needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Approval">
      <data key="d0">Request Approval</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Approval is the process of obtaining authorization for an analytics request. It is typically handled by the person in the reporting line who has the authority to approve the work.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Reprioritization">
      <data key="d0">Request Reprioritization</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Reprioritization is the process of adjusting the order in which analytics requests are handled. It is managed by the person in the reporting line who has the authority to reprioritize work.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Communication">
      <data key="d0">Request Communication</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Communication is the process of keeping stakeholders informed about the status and outcome of an analytics request. It is an important part of maintaining transparency and trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Ownership">
      <data key="d0">Request Ownership</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Ownership is the responsibility of a person from the requesting team to manage the analytics request and ensure that it is handled effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Context">
      <data key="d0">Request Context</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Context refers to the background and details provided with an analytics request. It includes information about the products or services affected, the planning horizon, and any known disruptions.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Description">
      <data key="d0">Request Description</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Description is the explanation of the analytics request, including the decision being made, what success looks like, and when the results are needed.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Timing">
      <data key="d0">Request Timing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Timing refers to the schedule or deadline for an analytics request. It is important to communicate when the results are needed to ensure timely delivery.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Request Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Evaluation is the process of assessing the feasibility and scope of an analytics request. It may involve suggesting a smaller first step to deliver value sooner.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Feedback">
      <data key="d0">Request Feedback</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Feedback is the input provided by the Dankenor Analytics Unit on an analytics request. It may include suggestions for scoping, adjustments, or improvements to the request.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Outcome">
      <data key="d0">Request Outcome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Outcome is the result of an analytics request. It is shared with the requesting team and the Dankenor Analytics Unit to ensure that the work is used effectively and to inform future projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Resolution">
      <data key="d0">Request Resolution</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Resolution is the process of completing an analytics request and delivering the results. It includes sharing the outcome and ensuring that the work meets the needs of the requesting team.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Tracking">
      <data key="d0">Request Tracking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Tracking is the process of monitoring the status of an analytics request. It ensures that the work is progressing and that stakeholders are informed of any changes or updates.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Escalation">
      <data key="d0">Request Escalation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Escalation is the process of bringing an analytics request to the attention of higher-level stakeholders or managers. It is used when there are issues with approval, prioritization, or communication.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Assignment">
      <data key="d0">Request Assignment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Assignment is the process of identifying the right person or team to handle an analytics request. It ensures that the work is assigned to the most appropriate specialist or workstream.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Closure">
      <data key="d0">Request Closure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Closure is the process of finalizing an analytics request and ensuring that all deliverables have been met. It includes sharing the outcome and confirming that the work has been used effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request Follow-Up">
      <data key="d0">Request Follow-Up</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Request Follow-Up is the process of checking in on the outcome of an analytics request and ensuring that the work has been used as intended. It helps build trust and ensures that the unit's work continues to add value.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
