    <node id="Liluan Nemlurel">
      <data key="d0">Liluan Nemlurel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Liluan Nemlurel is a long-tenured employee who has been with Zastama Industries since 2016 and serves as a key contributor to the company's technical and operational development. As a Solutions Architect, Liluan is responsible for technical ownership and integration planning at the Tegurine Annex, and acts as the first point of contact for design-related questions. In this role, they ensure that cost implications are addressed with the appropriate budget holders, demonstrating a strong commitment to both technical and financial accountability.

Liluan is also a member of the Talhuor Integration Team and holds an access badge series ME-4261-M, indicating their level of access and involvement in critical integration processes. Their expertise extends to demand forecasting models, an area in which they focus extensively. Liluan is tasked with preparing a walkthrough of their assumptions and limitations related to these models, highlighting their analytical and communicative skills. As a participant in relevant meetings, they contribute insights that reflect both their deep technical knowledge and their role as a source of institutional memory regarding the evolution of company practices.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialist at Zastama Industries working on demand forecasting models and collaborating with the planning group.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-009-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-003-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-004&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-006&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-009&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-008&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-002&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-003&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-003</data>
      <data key="d5">1793469151</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
