    <node id="Facilities Planning Lead">
      <data key="d0">Facilities Planning Lead</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Facilities Planning Lead is an individual tasked with reviewing current seat assignments at the Renzer Field Office and identifying underused seats to optimize physical capacity for the Feltarel Relay launch.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Workforce Operations Lead">
      <data key="d0">Workforce Operations Lead</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Workforce Operations Lead is an individual responsible for consolidating a draft list of roles expected to be on-site during the Feltarel Relay launch period and identifying which roles could work remotely.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Director, Program Operations">
      <data key="d0">Director, Program Operations</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Director of Program Operations is the author of the memo and is responsible for ensuring that the surrounding conditions for the Feltarel Relay launch are ready, including space, access, and coordination of support staff.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Paskian Platform Group">
      <data key="d0">Paskian Platform Group</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Paskian Platform Group is the team responsible for the technical development of the Feltarel Relay and owns the work leading up to its launch.&lt;SEP&gt;A group within Zastama Industries responsible for managing data retention tooling and related efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of 16 people responsible for the development of the Gaskergur Harbor at Zastama Industries. The group focuses on stabilizing core components, reducing defect backlogs, and addressing audit findings.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-007-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-001-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-007&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-001</data>
      <data key="d5">1793469298</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SJ-7058-R">
      <data key="d0">SJ-7058-R</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">SJ-7058-R is the contract number under which the Feltarel Relay is administered. It is to be referenced for all purchasing, staffing, or facilities requests related to the program.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seating and Staffing Plan">
      <data key="d0">Seating and Staffing Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Seating and Staffing Plan is a document to be consolidated by the Director, Program Operations, based on inputs from the Facilities Planning Lead, Workforce Operations Lead, and Program Leadership Group. It will outline the seating and staffing arrangements for the Feltarel Relay launch.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Launch Period">
      <data key="d0">Launch Period</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Launch Period refers to the time during which the Feltarel Relay will be launched, requiring coordination of on-site and remote staff, as well as space and access planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contract">
      <data key="d0">Contract</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A contract is a formal agreement under which the Feltarel Relay is administered, identified by the number SJ-7058-R. It governs purchasing, staffing, and facilities requests related to the program.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Remote Participation">
      <data key="d0">Remote Participation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Remote Participation is an alternative arrangement for staff who may not need to be physically present at the Renzer Field Office during the Feltarel Relay launch period.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Staggered Schedules">
      <data key="d0">Staggered Schedules</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staggered Schedules are an alternative planning approach to manage seating capacity at the Renzer Field Office by rotating staff presence during the Feltarel Relay launch period.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alternative Arrangements">
      <data key="d0">Alternative Arrangements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Alternative Arrangements are contingency plans to be considered if the seating capacity at the Renzer Field Office cannot accommodate all required staff for the Feltarel Relay launch.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planning Review">
      <data key="d0">Planning Review</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Planning Review is a scheduled meeting where the consolidated seating and staffing plan for the Feltarel Relay will be reviewed by the recipients of the memo.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visiting Colleagues">
      <data key="d0">Visiting Colleagues</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Visiting Colleagues are individuals who are temporarily present at the Renzer Field Office and are part of the existing occupants to be considered in seating capacity planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contractors">
      <data key="d0">Contractors</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Contractors are individuals hired for specific tasks and are part of the existing occupants to be considered in seating capacity planning at the Renzer Field Office.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Support Staff">
      <data key="d0">Support Staff</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Support Staff are individuals who will be present at the Renzer Field Office during the Feltarel Relay launch period to assist with the project, either permanently or on a rotating basis.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rotating Basis">
      <data key="d0">Rotating Basis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Rotating Basis refers to the temporary or intermittent presence of support staff at the Renzer Field Office during the Feltarel Relay launch period.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_a-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_a-002</data>
      <data key="d5">1793350812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Logistics">
      <data key="d0">Logistics</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Logistics refers to the coordination of space, access, and staffing to ensure that the Paskian Platform Group is not slowed down during the development and launch of the Feltarel Relay.</data>
