      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Finance Lead">
      <data key="d0">Finance Lead</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Finance Lead is a role typically held by an individual responsible for overseeing financial processes and ensuring alignment between technical decisions and budget tracking, particularly within specific projects or organizations such as Zastama Industries. The Finance Lead is tasked with confirming that received items match what has been approved for payment and ensuring that charges for restricted access group work are correctly assigned to designated budget codes, such as GW-2651-D during transitions. This role also involves tracking contract values against approved allocations, such as the $3.4M contract, and ensuring that the budget of specific projects, like Project Pirpoan, remains aligned with its approved amount.

In addition to budget tracking, the Finance Lead is responsible for confirming that escrow arrangements are properly documented and that the correct individuals hold relevant references. The role also includes consulting on pending integration costs that may need to be flagged ahead of the next planning cycle. As a stakeholder in various projects, including Project Siduris and Project Kridresa, the Finance Lead is expected to be briefed, not raise blocking objections, and participate in regular check-ins to confirm expectations and scope alignment. Overall, the Finance Lead plays a critical role in maintaining financial integrity and ensuring that financial decisions support project objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;A stakeholder in the Gaskergur Harbor project who provides input on payments reconciliation policy and is involved in reviewing design notes.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-team_b-001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-009-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-001-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-team_b-001&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-004&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-008&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-002&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-003&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-009&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-001</data>
      <data key="d5">1793469298</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
